<article class="env-theorem" id="0DIG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DIG">Theorem <span data-tag="0DIG">38.29.6</span> <span class="named">(Derived Grothendieck Existence Theorem)</span>.</a>  In Situation <a href="/tag/0DIB" data-tag="0DIB">38.29.1</a> there exists a pseudo-coherent $K$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ such that $K_ n = K \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X}^\mathbf {L} \mathcal{O}_{X_ n}$ for all $n$ compatibly with the maps $\varphi _ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemmas <a href="/tag/0DIC" data-tag="0DIC">38.29.2</a>, <a href="/tag/0DID" data-tag="0DID">38.29.3</a>, <a href="/tag/0DIE" data-tag="0DIE">38.29.4</a> to get a pseudo-coherent object $K$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Choosing affine opens in Lemma <a href="/tag/0DIF" data-tag="0DIF">38.29.5</a> it follows immediately that $K$ restricts to $K_ n$ over $X_ n$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>